---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Arm-Friendly Pickleball Paddle Tips | PaddleFitHub"
  description="Learn how to choose arm-friendly pickleball paddle specs. Tips on weight, core thickness, grip size, and vibration control for comfortable play."
  canonicalPath="/blog/arm-friendly-paddle-tips/"
>
  <div class="container-narrow py-16">
    <p class="text-caption-mono text-mute uppercase tracking-wide mb-2">Resource</p>
    <h1 class="text-display-xl text-ink mb-4">Arm-Friendly Paddle Tips</h1>
    <p class="text-body-lg text-body mb-8">The right paddle specs can make a real difference in playing comfort. Here are the key factors to consider.</p>

    <div class="prose text-body-md text-body space-y-6 max-w-none">
      <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">Weight matters</h2>
      <p>Ultralight paddles (under 7.0 oz) can transmit more vibration. A moderate weight (7.5 – 8.0 oz) provides stability that helps absorb impact shock. Very heavy paddles (over 8.5 oz) can increase cumulative fatigue.</p>

      <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">Thicker cores absorb vibration</h2>
      <p>A 16 mm or 20 mm core dampens more vibration than a thin 14 mm core. If arm comfort is a priority, avoid the thinnest cores.</p>

      <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">Grip size is critical</h2>
      <p>A grip that is too small increases wrist torque; one that is too large forces you to grip tighter. Both can aggravate arm issues. Use the <a href="/tools/grip-size-calculator/">Grip Size Calculator</a> to check your fit.</p>

      <h2 class="text-display-sm text-ink">Shape and balance</h2>
      <p>Standard and hybrid shapes offer larger sweet spots, meaning fewer off-center hits that send shock through the arm. A handle-heavy balance can also reduce impact strain.</p>

      <p class="mt-6 p-4 bg-warning-soft/30 rounded-md text-body-sm">This information is for general guidance only and is not medical advice. If you are experiencing persistent arm pain, consult a healthcare professional.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-hairline">
      <a href="/tools/arm-friendly-paddle-finder/" class="btn-primary">Try the Arm-Friendly Paddle Finder</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>